  "title": "Erdős Problem #1072",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For any prime $p$, let $f(p)$ be the least integer such that $f(p)!+1\\equiv 0\\pmod{p}$.\nIs it true that there are infinitely many $p$ for which $f(p)=p-1$?\nIs it true that $f(p)/p\\to 0$ for almost all $p$?",
